A||||3||SLYGUY||Notchy shiftin'...||||13||
Z||000000||SLYGUY||10-04-2001||03:44 AM||||Shifting my GT is a notchy affair. <BR>When you first start the engine, let it warm a little, you have to have the clutch buried into the bulkhead to select first. As soon as you reach operating temp it is easier, but remains notchy.<P>Car:<BR>1988 Fiero GT<BR>2.8 V6<BR>5spd<P>Tranny fluid (5W motor oil) new<BR>Clutch fluid reservoir at right level<P>The motor oil I used was listed in the Haynes manual.<BR>Should I use a thinner or thicker fluid?<P>Sly<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000001||RossT||10-04-2001||04:47 AM||||Sometime in 1988 GM changed the fluid recomended fluid to "synchromesh" It is a GM<BR>synthetic fluid that you can buy at the dealrship for about 14 bucks a bottle.  It takes exactly two bottles.<P>I would start by bleeding your clutch with new DOT 3 brake fluid and changing the tranny fluid back to synchromesh.  I have the GM part number somewhere if you need it.<P>Then check for improvement.<P>Check <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>  for instructions on clutch bleeding.  I personally use a mytivac<BR>vacuum tool to do mine, but Achies way requires no tool.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||10-04-2001||10:46 PM||||I'd wait and see what THE OGRE has to say about it... I  remember him declaring synthetic fluids a hazard a while ago. He's the undisputed KING of the Fiero fluid systems  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>OGRE? I summon thee! Here's a mystical pack of smokes and a cheap gold watch! DO MY BIDDING!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||10-05-2001||07:14 AM||||"GM Syncromesh" I belive is a natural Petrol-based transmission lube, with syncro addatives added for increased friction (yes, friction)  AFAIK, no component is truely 'synthetic'<P><BR>I have had great success with Red Line's MTL" product, a special synthetic lubricant, again with the special (and *QUITE* nessicary) Friction addatives that ensure proper syncro engaugement and spin rates.  It is also designed with the shear-forces of gear teath in mind, as opposed to only bearing surfaces in an engine.<P>Synthetic motor oils are just plain too slipry.<P><BR>Replace fluid with RedLine or the GM stuff, and your woes will go away.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
